{
  "schemaVersion": 2,
  "name": "Utopia City Implementation",
  "description": "Actual implementation layer of the Utopia Digital City. The Digital-City repository stays the map/planning reference; this tree owns the running modules. Only districts that really exist are listed. A module may be strengthened by several incubation rooms over time, so it records incubationRooms[] rather than a single roomId. Two incubation identities are recognised: a Room Pack incubator room (apps/rooms/rooms/<id>, recorded in apps/rooms/promotions/<id>.json) and a mission-book migration incubator, whose id has the form mb-<MISSION_ID>-<module>-lab and which MUST be accompanied by a module.mission block naming the mission and the cluster it migrated. The second form exists because Digital-City/mission-book is a separate, Owner-defined control plane: it lands code directly under city/ on a mission/<MISSION_ID>-<slug> branch, accepted by a second host, instead of incubating a live Room first.",
  "lifecycles": [
    "PLANNED",
